userStories.description:
**Goal** — Pass the resolved enforcement policy into StaticRulesProvider and surface canonical-rule budget pressure alongside its emitted chunks.

**Motivation** — The loss is unmetered: `static-rules.ts:245-252` logs a warning carrying `droppedCount`, but nothing reaches `StoryMetrics`.

**Approach** — `StaticRulesProvider.fetch()` consumes the `applyCanonicalRulesBudget` result and returns `ContextProviderResult{chunks, budgetPressure?}`. The provider emits full pressure only when its canonical-rule total is over the configured threshold.

**Scope** — In: add an enforceBudget provider option, pass it from the default orchestrator's resolved rules config, call the US-002 budget function with it, add `ContextProviderResult.budgetPressure`, and report pressure for soft and enforced over-budget results. Out: moving manifest types (US-001); persisting provider pressure in manifests and aggregating it into story metrics (US-004); Two-tier rule delivery — an always-on tier carrying every rule's prohibitions plus full text fetched on demand via a `query_rules` pull tool — is deferred to a later arc; it requires authored per-rule summaries and should be designed against measurements this feature produces. Fixing `ruleMatchesTouchedFiles` returning true when `touchedFiles` is empty (`static-rules.ts:141`), which makes `appliesTo:` inert for stories declaring no context files, is deferred to the scoping arc.

**Interface** —
```typescript
/** A provider's own budget pressure — how far over, and what it discarded. */
interface ProviderBudgetPressure {
  /** max(0, produced - providerBudget). Non-zero whenever the provider is over. */
  overageTokens: number;
  /** Items discarded to satisfy the budget. Zero unless the budget is enforced. */
  droppedCount: number;
  droppedTokens: number;
  /** Stable ids of discarded items, for manifest-level debugging. */
  droppedIds: string[];
}
```

`ContextProviderResult.budgetPressure?: ProviderBudgetPressure` carries the full shape. `droppedTokens` is the token total for omitted canonical rules and `droppedIds` uses canonical rule IDs. Omit `budgetPressure` when total canonical-rule tokens are within the provider budget. `NeutralityLintError` continues to propagate unchanged.

**File-size constraint** — `src/context/engine/types.ts` is at 590 lines against the 600-line `SRC_LIMIT` enforced by `scripts/check-file-sizes.ts` in `bun run lint`. This story depends on US-001, which relieves that file first. Declare `ProviderBudgetPressure` in `src/context/engine/manifest-types.ts` (created by US-001) and import it into `types.ts` so only the import line and the optional field land in `types.ts`. Do not re-inline the interface into `types.ts`.
